{
  "default": true,
  "locale": "en",
  "scene": "scn_b4t9ehwb",
  "schema": "patter/strings@0",
  "strings": {
    "L_5fyzfhq5": "Tonight, the fog will roll back in again, and more people will need your guidance to find safe harbour on these rocks.",
    "L_5y5qgsun": "But for now, the whole day is ahead of you.",
    "L_7xydcvlr": "It must be nearly 10 o'clock. You look out over the waves at the distant horizon.",
    "L_7yx41p3c": "You feel Shelly's lighter in your pocket. She was finally able to choose her own path. Like the mermaid she admired, she's now a creature of the waves, lingering in the place she loved most.",
    "L_9h05bn3d": "You're not sure what awaits Shelly in the world beyond, or if there even is one. But she had to move on. She couldn't have lingered here forever... could she? You hope you were right to give her that push.",
    "L_cois0olq": "You remember Rupert's face, transformed by the belief that Johnathon and many more besides were given a second chance at life thanks to the antitoxin. You even think you remember the empty lamp he held flare gold for a spell before he moved on to... elsewhere.",
    "L_sfoian5r": "Theo's spirit now is finally at rest. As you look to the sky and feel the breeze, you are reminded of the sad miller's story. Maybe this memory too is a legacy of a sort. The echo of the Montgomery family is still felt clearly in this little town.",
    "L_tsscwz4l": "You wish you could have gotten through to Theo. But the cycle of sadness and guilt is a chain not so easily broken. Maybe at some point Theo will find peace with what happened. But until that day, the legacy of the Montgomery family lingers in those isolated crags.",
    "L_wjzk9mmr": "Rupert's words, tinged with grief and hope, stay with you. The world might be crumbling, but at the end, you can only make do with the time you have. You hope Rupert finds peace knowing Johnathon may have survived.  ",
    "L_xbxyfirl": "Occasionally, when you walk by the site of the old lighthouse keeper's house, you smell the alluring wafts of Rupert's 'welcome home' supper. You don't suppose this ghost will ever move on, not without his brother.   ",
  },
}
